ubscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2020-09-28T21:38:04Z", "updated_at": "2020-09-28T21:38:04Z", "body": "I am using that GPS data as a reference point, which my other applications will rely on. I did get some answer from px4 perspective [here](https://discuss.px4.io/t/difference-between-gps-altitude-vs-fused-altiude-estimation/18784), seems the fused data also consider other sensors. \r\n\r\nSo the question becomes is there any method for MAVSDK to access the raw data, not fused ones?\r\n\r\nAlso, I notice in MAVLink message definition, there are [GPS_RAW_INT](https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#GPS_RAW_INT) and [GLOBAL_POSITION_INT](https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#GLOBAL_POSITION_INT). Does MAVSDK provide any api to access that?\r\n", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/700294927/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null, "event": "commented", "actor": {"login": "cjffly", "id": 11035640, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjExMDM1NjQw", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11035640?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly", "html_url": "https://github.com/cjffly", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/703437079", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1198#issuecomment-703437079", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1198", "id": 703437079, "node_id": "MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDcwMzQzNzA3OQ==", "user": {"login": "julianoes", "id": 1419688, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTk2ODg=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1419688?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes", "html_url": "https://github.com/julianoes", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2020-10-05T06:53:34Z", "updated_at": "2020-10-05T06:54:36Z", "body": "@cjffly if you are using MAVSDK C++ you can use the Passthrough plugin to access any MAVLink message. So that would be one way. Alternatively, you can make a pull request to 